#: ../../source/start/first-run.md:1
msgid "A first run, argument by argument"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md:3
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Assuming {doc}`install` is done and the two {doc}`../guides/user/inputs` "
"exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md:15
msgid "Line by line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md:17
msgid "`--input report.pdf`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md:18
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"the document. A bare path here means *this local file*, made absolute, "
"and its own text becomes the document's **name** — the value that will "
"appear in the `Report` column of the output. Give it a shorter one with "
"`report.pdf:EURIZON 2023`, which you will want as soon as there are two "
"documents. The full grammar is in {doc}`../guides/user/documents`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md:23
msgid "`--format EURIZON-EN23`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md:24
msgid ""
"which recipe to read it with. Omissible **only** when the document came "
"from a URL the formats repository's mapping recognises; a local path "
"carries no evidence of who published it. Naming a format the repository "
"does not have is an error naming the format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md:28
msgid "`--repo ~/work/formats-repo`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md:29
msgid ""
"the formats repository. Also `--formats-directory`, `-F`, `-r`, or "
"`FREEPORTS_FORMATS_REPO_PATH`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md:31
msgid "`--db-directory ~/work/input-db`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md:32
msgid "the input database. Also `-I`, or `FREEPORTS_INPUT_DB_PATH`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md:34
msgid "`--target-list controversial_weapons`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md:35
msgid ""
"which list of companies to look for. Repeatable. **Without it the run "
"stops immediately**, before opening the PDF — the presence check runs "
"first on purpose, so a missing input fails in a second rather than after "
"four minutes of PDF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md:39
msgid "`--out ./results`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md:40
msgid ""
"where the tables go. A directory for the default profile. Defaults to the"
" working directory, so omitting it is legal and rarely what you want."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md:43
msgid "What the run produced"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md:52
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Nine tables and an audit trail. Most runs care about `investments.csv` — "
"one row per holding — and the rest describe the funds those holdings "
"belong to. Every CSV has its header even when it has no rows, so "
"*\"nothing found\"* and *\"no such table\"* stay distinguishable. "
"{doc}`../guides/user/output` is the full list and the rules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md:57
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`.log.csv` is not an output table: it is the extraction's own record of "
"what it skipped and where. It lands **next to the output** because it is "
"a product of the run. {doc}`../guides/user/logging` explains how to read "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md:61
msgid "Adding a second document"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md:67
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Two jobs, one run, **one** set of tables, with the `Report` column "
"telling the rows apart. This is not the same as two separate runs "
"concatenated: in one invocation the two documents share promise "
"resolution and fund deduplication. See "
"{doc}`../reference/design/multidocument`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md:71
msgid "When the first run does not work"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md
msgid "Symptom"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md
msgid "Usually"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md
msgid "stops at once, says a target list is missing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md
msgid "`--target-list` not given — the first check"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md
msgid "runs, finds nothing, writes header-only tables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md
msgid ""
"the format is right but the companies are not in the named list, or the "
"list is empty"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md
msgid "a format error naming a format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md
msgid "the name is not in the repository's `metadata/formats.csv`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md
msgid "holdings attributed to the wrong company"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"the input database's order, not the extraction — see "
"{doc}`../guides/user/inputs`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/first-run.md:79
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Raise the verbosity before guessing: `-v` narrates the run, `-vv` and "
"`-vvv` more. {doc}`../guides/user/logging`."
msgstr ""

